  "centre_line_x": 45.0,
  "steering_notes": "lateral_axis is glTF world -X (skier faces +Z, so their right is -X); the steer node is a child of the trajectory root, so its local X should be driven with the same sign. Half widths are measured from the jump centre line (x = 45) to the edge of the skiable snow surface: inrun snow 3.8 m (concrete side walls and handrails at 4.3 m); landing is the narrowest point at the knoll, widening downhill per landing_half_width_profile_m. The skier itself is ~0.43 m half-wide.",
